<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles IV</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Emperor Charles IV</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles IV was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> in the fourteenth century and king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>. In 1356 he issued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356">Golden Bull</a>, which codified the election of the emperor by seven <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a>. The document defined the constitutional structure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> for centuries.</p></div>
